extraction_notes: |
  Read from Rifts World Book 6: South America printed 114-115 (cache p115-p116).
  The class heading and first lore paragraph sit at the foot of printed 114;
  printed 115 holds the rest. Printed 116 (cache p117) is the Sekhmet and is
  not part of this class, so source_book is p.114-115. Cache p116 is on the
  corrupt_pages list: every number on printed 115 was read off a 170 dpi render,
  and all agreed with the text layer except the force-field cost, which the
  text layer reads "101.S.P." and the render shows 10 I.S.P.

  1. XP_TABLE is the ladder "Flame Panther, Flying Tiger & Oracle Cat" on
     printed 168 (cache p169), checked against a render. Lower bounds as
     printed: 0, 2,201, 4,401 ... 343,001.
  2. DIVINE ORACLE is not a separate class. The book says oracle cats who
     become priests of the Divine Felines gain clerical powers, use the Priest
     O.C.C. skills (Rifts Conversion Book Two) and need twice the experience of
     the oracle cat R.C.C. per level. Recorded in GM Notes; nothing stored.
  3. POOLS. Hit points "P.E. plus 1D6 per level". S.D.C. "1D4X10 plus those
     gained through skills" is sdc_base, as other stand-alone Rifts R.C.C.s with
     their own skill lists store it; no men_of_arms line because sdc_base is
     stated. The printed "M.D.C." is only the psionic force field (10 per
     level), so no mdc_base; it is a special ability. P.P.E. 2D6.
  4. PSIONICS. Master. I.S.P. "M.E. attribute plus 4D6X10, add 10 per
     additional level". The eight inborn powers are granted by name; See the
     Invisible is the catalog''s See The Invisible. Empathic Transmission is a
     Super power, so Super is in categories_allowed.
  5. ADDITIONAL POWERS. "At every level starting with the second": two from
     Sensitive, Physical or Healing, or one Super. "After reaching fifth level":
     two lesser plus one Super. Decision: levels 2-4 use the first rule and
     levels 5-15 the second, reading "after reaching fifth level" as including
     fifth. The either/or at 2-4 cannot be filtered, so it is one two-pick
     entry reaching all four categories with a note that a Super power takes
     both picks.
  6. SKILLS. Basic and Advanced Math (+20%) is two rows, Mathematics: Basic and
     Mathematics: Advanced, each 45+20. Lore: Demons and Monsters is the
     catalog''s Lore: Demons & Monsters. Ancient Egyptian (+30%) has no catalog
     row and is a fixed Language: Other at 80 naming the tongue; the language
     of choice is a separate Language: Other pick at +15%. Literacy (+10%)
     names no language and is the catalog''s plain Literacy row at 30+10.
     Paramedic 40+20.
  7. HAND TO HAND: the book grants Martial Arts, or Assassin if evil, and
     prints no upgrade price, so no hand_to_hand block.
  8. RELATED AND SECONDARY SKILLS are stored because this R.C.C. prints its own
     O.C.C.-style lists: six related picks plus one at levels 3, 5, 7, 11 and
     15, and four secondary plus two at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12. Mechanical and
     Military are "None" and are left out of both lists. Science is Astronomy
     only; Physical excludes Boxing and Wrestling. Secondary picks follow the
     same categories and restrictions without the bonuses.
  9. BONUSES: the book prints none for the race beyond its abilities; the +2
     save in Aura of Peace belongs to the targets and is prose.
  10. EQUIPMENT. Light M.D.C. body armor is the catalog''s generic light suit;
      the book gives this one 30 M.D.C., in the note. The light energy weapon
      and TW weapon are unnamed in the book, so each is a choice from catalog
      rows led by this book''s own weapons. "Assorted survival equipment" is the
      Survival Kit row.
  11. MONEY. The book prints 2D6X1000 in salable items. Salable goods are not
      coin, so starting_money is not stored (as with the Sekhmet and Flame
      Panther); the restriction line records the 2D6x1000.
