# Oracle Cat

## Lore

Oracle cats are the descendants of Zee and the rest of the ZB-23 genetic batch, felinoid mutants of Omagua. They look almost like cartoons: oversized heads, small furry bodies and big round innocent eyes that remind humans of stuffed toys. That harmless look hides enormous psionic power. They glimpse future events, read minds, and can calm berserk animals and monsters, including the hunter cats.

Most are pillars of the community and the most respected felinoid race in the city, serving as war leaders, military advisors, paramedics, doctors, judges, spies and security officers. A few turn to crime.

## GM Notes

Divine Oracles are oracle cats who have become priests of the Divine Felines. They hold both psionic and clerical powers, use the Priest O.C.C. skill list (Rifts Conversion Book Two) instead of the oracle cat''s, and need twice the experience per level that an ordinary oracle cat does. They are revered as saints and chosen leaders, take part only in the most important missions, and are often sent across the Megaverse on their gods'' business. This is not a separate class here.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'oracle-cat');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'oracle-cat';

